To make all `<h2>` headings orange using CSS, you can define a new class in your CSS file or within a `<style>` tag in your HTML document. Here's how you can do it:

```css
.h2-orange {
    color: orange;
}
```

Or, if you prefer to use the hexadecimal color code for orange (which is #FFA500), you can specify it directly:

```css
.h2-orange {
    color: #FFA500;
}
```

Then, to apply this class to all `<h2>` headings, you would add the class attribute to each `<h2>` element in your HTML like so:

```html
<h2 class="h2-orange">This is an H2 heading</h2>
```

Alternatively, if you want to apply the style globally to all `<h2>` elements without needing to add a class to each one, you can use a `*` selector in your CSS:

```css
h2 {
    color: orange;
}
```

This will apply the orange color to all `<h2>` elements on the page without needing to manually add the class to each one.

